come", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01TPfMpBmcW28cQkuD5m8vKf", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55787, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TPfMpBmcW28cQkuD5m8vKf", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60295, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Version choice:** The release history wasn't listed in order. Sorted by deploy order, it goes v2.2.9 (healthy) \u2192 v2.3.0 (healthy) \u2192 v2.3.1-rc (unhealthy) \u2192 v2.3.1 (unhealthy). So v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) had been running v2.3.1 with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0. A follow-up status check shows the service healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback and the recovered health. It notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again. Opening it paged the on-call engineer.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WEfwP8fELCmm191BZN8bEb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TpsR3baZQV1gybvyaDJK2u", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": 